--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Unreal Engine content and template code (Unreal Engine EULA, not MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following come from Epic Games' Unreal Engine and its Top Down template,
or are built from them. They are NOT licensed under the MIT License above.
They remain subject to the Unreal Engine End User License Agreement
(https://www.unrealengine.com/eula/unreal), and you may only use them as that
agreement allows:

- Everything in MultiplayerGame/Content/: the Top Down template maps,
  blueprints and cursor, the LevelPrototyping assets, and the Mannequin and
  Mannequin_UE4 characters, animations, materials and rigs.
- The Top Down template source files marked "Copyright Epic Games, Inc.":
  MultiplayerGame.h/.cpp, MultiplayerGameCharacter.h/.cpp,
  MultiplayerGameGameMode.h/.cpp, MultiplayerGamePlayerController.h/.cpp,
  MultiplayerGame.Build.cs and the *.Target.cs files.
- The project and config files generated from the template
  (MultiplayerGame.uproject, MultiplayerGame.sln, MultiplayerGame/Config/),
  apart from the Edgegap sections listed in section 1.

Unreal Engine itself is not included in this repository. Building and running
this sample requires Unreal Engine, which is licensed separately by Epic Games
under the same EULA.
